# Windows batch files must check out with CRLF endings. cmd.exe can mis-parse
# labels and goto targets in an LF-only .bat, and it fails at runtime rather
# than at parse time. This repo is authored on Linux (jhm-spark) and run on
# Windows, so the conversion has to be declared rather than assumed.
#
# Deliberately scoped to *.bat only. A blanket `* text=auto` would renormalise
# line endings across every tracked file on the next commit, which would show up
# as hundreds of spurious modifications in a repo this size.
*.bat text eol=crlf
